@@ -445,6 +447,23 @@ For example if your position adjustment assumes it can do 2 additional buys with
 
 Or another example if your position adjustment assumes it can do 1 additional buy with 3x the original stake amount then `custom_stake_amount` should return 25% of proposed stake amount and leave 75% for possible later position adjustments.
 
+#### Limiting exposure to a single underlying currency
+
+If you trade several pairs that are all priced against (or, for futures, margined in) the same currency - for example several coins quoted in the same stablecoin, or a handful of futures margined in the same currency - a single adverse move in that currency can hit several of your open trades at once, even though each trade looked fine in isolation.
+
+`max_currency_exposure` limits how much of your tradable capital may be committed at any one time to trades sharing the same underlying (quote/margin) currency. It's expressed as a ratio of the [total tradable stake amount](#tradable-balance) (`0.5` = at most 50% of tradable capital in one underlying currency).
+
+```json
+"max_currency_exposure": 0.5,
+```
+
+When opening (or adding to) a trade would push the combined stake amount committed to that currency above the configured ratio, the stake amount is reduced to fit under the limit - the same way stake amounts are already adjusted to fit `stake_available` or the exchange's max stake amount. If the limit is already reached, the resulting stake amount is `0` and the trade is skipped. The reason is logged exactly like other entry-sizing adjustments.
+
+This option can be set in the configuration or in the strategy ([Strategy Override](#parameters-in-the-strategy)), and applies identically in live/dry-run trading and in backtesting/hyperopt, since both use the same wallet sizing logic.
+
+!!! Note
+    This is disabled (no cap) by default.
+
